## User Review Required

> [!NOTE]
> In Pass 1, Coventry collapses to the attack boundary ($\alpha = 0.01$) because it scored 0 goals in 3 matches, and Hull collapses to defense boundary ($\beta = 0.01$) because it conceded 0 goals in 3 matches.
> In Pass 2, pinning their parameters to empirical priors ($P_{25}^{\text{att}} = 0.6097$, $P_{75}^{\text{def}} = 1.9590$) via L-BFGS-B parameter bounds `(prior, prior)` and warm-starting from Pass 1 converges in ~0.74s, shifting $\gamma$ from $1.2018 \to 1.1853$ and $\rho$ from $-0.1432 \to -0.1359$. This guarantees a single coherent joint MLE.

