## Proposed Changes

### Machine Learning Models

#### [MODIFY] [ml/models/dixon_coles.py](file:///d:/Yash/Kokane/Projects/MatchSense/ml/models/dixon_coles.py)
- In `DixonColesModel.fit()`:
  - After Pass 1 optimization converges, inspect small-sample teams ($< 5$ matches in training window).
  - If any small-sample team has collapsed to $\le 0.15$ for attack or defense:
    - Compute empirical priors from established teams ($\ge 10$ matches): $P_{25}$ for attack, $P_{75}$ for defense.
    - Set parameter bounds for the collapsed parameters to `(prior, prior)` and initialize them at `prior`.
    - Execute Pass 2 with `scipy.optimize.minimize` (L-BFGS-B) warm-started from Pass 1 parameters.
    - Unpack Pass 2 parameters into `self._attack, self._defense, self._home_advantage, self._rho`.
    - Log Pass 2 iterations, time, and parameter shifts ($\Delta\gamma, \Delta\rho$).

